{
  "model": "IndexTeam/IndexTTS-2.5",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "pause_seconds": 0.7,
  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "s53-p01",
      "text": "Look at the Earth from space.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p02",
      "text": "Our planet looks so blue, because water covers nearly three quarters of its surface.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p03",
      "text": "Water is an important part of our body, too.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p03.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p03.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p04",
      "text": "More than half of our total body weight is water.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p04.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p04.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p05",
      "text": "Our body loses water whenever we play sports like football, or go to the toilet.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p05.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p05.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p06",
      "text": "That's why we need to drink plenty of water every day.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p06.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p06.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p07",
      "text": "We use water to cook, clean, and we then carry waste out of our homes.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p07.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p07.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p08",
      "text": "We use it to take a bath or wash dishes and chopsticks in the kitchen.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p08.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p08.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p09",
      "text": "Farmers use it to grow crops like rice, corn, carrots and tomatoes; factories use it to make products.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p09.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p09.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p10",
      "text": "Since the 1950s, as the population grew, the amount of water that people have used has increased by three times.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p10.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p10.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p11",
      "text": "But the water supply hasn't.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p11.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p11.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p12-01",
      "text": "Scientists worry that soon there won't be enough water for us,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p12-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p12-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p12-02",
      "text": "as well as for the animals and plants that share our world.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p12-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p12-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p13",
      "text": "What can we do to help?",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p13.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p13.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p14",
      "text": "Use water wisely.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p14.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p14.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p15",
      "text": "Not having enough water isn't the only problem that we need to solve.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p15.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p15.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p16",
      "text": "We also need it to be clean.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p16.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p16.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p17",
      "text": "Right now, ships and factories are putting wastes into seas, rivers and lakes.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p17.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p17.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p18",
      "text": "Even chemicals that farmers use are running into rivers and lakes.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p18.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p18.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p19",
      "text": "All this pollution can make the water dangerous to drink and cause diseases like cancer.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p19.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p19.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p20",
      "text": "It can also harm fish, whales and other aquatic life.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p20.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p20.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p21",
      "text": "We must do something to stop pollution.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p21.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p21.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s53-p22",
      "text": "It's the best way to protect our world's most valuable natural resource.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p22.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s53-p22.mp3"
    }
  ],
  "word_audio": "browser speech synthesis en-GB"
}
